{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "גוים", :translit "goyim", :gloss "nations"} {:he "גיים כתיב", :translit "geim katuv", :gloss "it is written geim"} {:he "רמז לעשרה אומות שבאו להחריב את בית המקדש", :translit "remez le'asarah umot sheba'u lehachriv et beit hamikdash", :gloss "allusion to ten nations that came to destroy the Temple"} {:he "אהלי אדום וישמעאלים", :translit "ohalei edom viyishma'elim", :gloss "tents of Edom and Ishmaelites"} {:he "והם יו״ד", :translit "vehem yud", :gloss "and they are yud"} {:he "גיים עולה ס״ג", :translit "geim oleh sag", :gloss "geim equals 63"} {:he "זה נתברך בן ס״ג", :translit "zeh nitbarach ben sag", :gloss "this one was blessed with a son of 63"} {:he "וזה בא בס״ג אומות", :translit "vezeh ba besag umot", :gloss "and this one came with 63 nations"} {:he "בחורבן בית שני", :translit "bechurban beit sheini", :gloss "in the destruction of the Second Temple"} {:he "דז׳ אומות נעקרו", :translit "dezet umot ne'akru", :gloss "for 7 nations were uprooted"} {:he "הכל ס״ג יחדו נאלחו", :translit "hakol sag yachdo nalchu", :gloss "they all together became joined: 63"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :notarikon, :word "גיים", :expansion ["אהלי" "אדום" "וגו'"]} {:kind :other, :note "גיים read as יו״ד alluding to ten nations; alternately גיים equals 63 matching Esau's line and Jacob's, with 63 = 70 nations minus 7 uprooted"} {:kind :other, :note "Rabbinic mnemonic: הכל ס״ג יחדו נאלחו encodes the recurring number 63 across both interpretations"}], :frame {:text "The tents of Edom are identified in Psalm 137:7 and Obadiah 1:1–4 as participants in the destruction of the First Temple; the rabbinic exposition of Psalm 83:7–9 (Tehillim) lists ten nations including Edom and Ishmael who conspire against Israel. The image of ten nations destroying the Temple builds on the identification of Esau with Rome/Edom and Ishmael found in rabbinic literature (e.g., the exchange between Rabbi Yehudah HaNasi and Antoninus in Avodah Zarah 10b–11a). The tradition of seven Canaanite nations appears in Deuteronomy 7:1, and the reckoning of seventy founding nations in Genesis 10 undergirds the calculation that after seven were uprooted, sixty-three remain.", :sources ["Psalm 137:7" "Obadiah 1:1–4" "Psalm 83:7–9" "Deuteronomy 7:1" "Genesis 10" "Avodah Zarah 10b–11a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "שני גוים בבטנך", :translit "shnei goyim bevitnekh", :gloss "two nations in your womb"} {:he "בגימטריא זה רבי יהודה ואנטונינוס", :translit "begimatria zeh rabbi yehudah ve'antoninus", :gloss "in gematria this is Rabbi Yehudah and Antoninus"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "שני גוים בבטנך", :b "רבי יהודה ואנטונינוס"}], :frame {:text "Rebbi (Rabbi Yehudah HaNasi) maintained a close bond with the Roman emperor Antoninus, a relationship treated at length in Avodah Zarah 10a–11b. The Talmud there records exchanges of gifts and favours; Genesis Rabbah 63:7 identifies Esau's descendants with Rome, so that Rebecca's oracle of two nations in the womb can be mapped onto the historical pair Rebbi and Antoninus as types of Jacob and Esau.", :sources ["Avodah Zarah 10a–11b" "Genesis Rabbah 63:7"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ולאום מלאום יאמץ", :translit "ule'om mi-le'om ye'ematz", :gloss "and one nation from the other shall prevail"} {:he "יגבר על חבירו ויחריבו", :translit "yigbor al chavero viyarchivo", :gloss "he shall overpower his fellow and destroy him"} {:he "אמלאה החרבה", :translit "emlah ha-charbah", :gloss "I will fill the desolation"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The letters of ולאום מלאום יאמץ are rearranged to spell אמלאה החרבה"}], :frame {:text "The Targum Onkelos on Genesis 25:23 renders the verse as 'one people shall be stronger than the other,' reading it as a prophecy of mutual destruction between the descendants of Jacob and Esau. The anagram אמלאה החרבה ('I will fill the desolation') echoes the language of destruction found in prophetic rebukes such as Ezekiel 35:14 and Isaiah 13:21, where the desolation of Edom is declared.", :sources ["Targum Onkelos Genesis 25:23" "Ezekiel 35:14" "Isaiah 13:21"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :notarikon, :word "גיים", :expansion ["אהלי" "אדום" "וגו'"], :initials ["א" "א" "ו"], :by :selah, :initials-match? false} {:kind :other, :note "גיים read as יו״ד alluding to ten nations; alternately גיים equals 63 matching Esau's line and Jacob's, with 63 = 70 nations minus 7 uprooted", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Rabbinic mnemonic: הכל ס״ג יחדו נאלחו encodes the recurring number 63 across both interpretations", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "שני גוים בבטנך", :a-value 502, :b "רבי יהודה ואנטונינוס", :b-value 490, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "The letters of ולאום מלאום יאמץ are rearranged to spell אמלאה החרבה", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:08:14.206791497Z", :model "glm-5.2"}